1
00:00:00,451 --> 00:00:03,061
Campus journeys should not depend on guesswork.

2
00:00:03,061 --> 00:00:08,002
Route Pulse helps operators test better transport plans with the fleet they already have.

3
00:00:08,002 --> 00:00:11,445
This demonstration uses a fictional campus and synthetic data.

4
00:00:13,043 --> 00:00:14,965
We start a real optimization run.

5
00:00:14,965 --> 00:00:20,731
It adjusts departures within allowed windows and reassigns existing vehicles, without adding buses.

6
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:24,451
The proposed plan changes twenty one duties.

7
00:00:24,451 --> 00:00:26,780
All ten hard constraint categories pass.

8
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,855
The operator can review the changes before accepting a recommendation.

9
00:00:31,305 --> 00:00:35,171
For a fair comparison, both plans face the same passengers and traffic.

10
00:00:35,171 --> 00:00:39,690
Completed journeys rise from seven hundred and six to eight hundred and forty nine.

11
00:00:39,690 --> 00:00:44,591
Average waiting falls from thirty five point three to twenty eight point zero six minutes.

12
00:00:45,041 --> 00:00:46,664
One good run is not enough.

13
00:00:46,664 --> 00:00:52,074
We freeze this proposal and evaluate it on twenty additional, prespecified synthetic days.

14
00:00:52,074 --> 00:00:56,583
The plan is not retuned between days, and the report retains every outcome.

15
00:01:01,349 --> 00:01:07,575
Completed journeys improve on all twenty days, averaging about one hundred and fifty additional journeys per day.

16
00:01:07,575 --> 00:01:11,377
But there is a trade off: missed connections worsen on thirteen days.

17
00:01:11,377 --> 00:01:14,793
Route Pulse makes that limitation visible alongside the gains.

18
00:01:19,449 --> 00:01:22,745
Aggregate improvements can hide harm to individual groups.

19
00:01:22,745 --> 00:01:30,986
The Evidence Lab breaks down service and waiting time by passenger origin, helping an operator investigate who benefits and who may be worse off.

20
00:01:34,815 --> 00:01:38,219
Arrival predictions are checked against simulated ground truth.

21
00:01:38,219 --> 00:01:41,569
Reports show measured errors and prediction interval coverage.

22
00:01:43,681 --> 00:01:47,781
The next step is a campus shadow pilot using real historical data.

23
00:01:47,781 --> 00:01:51,571
This prototype demonstrates a reproducible decision workflow.

24
00:01:51,571 --> 00:01:54,305
Benefits in a live campus remain unverified.
